=== SURVEY ===
Web source RateLimitBanner.tsx is an EVENT-DRIVEN, self-owning banner mounted in <Layout>. It owns its
visibility (`useState`) and a per-second countdown; its data arrives via two document CustomEvents:
  • teslasync:rate-limited  (429)  → State{kind:'rate-limited', scope, expiresAt}
  • teslasync:upstream-down  (503 UPSTREAM_BREAKER_OPEN) → State{kind:'upstream-down', upstream, expiresAt}
Render (when state != null):
  • icon: Clock (rate-limit) / AlertCircle (upstream); amber/warning chrome.
  • message: isRateLimit ? t('ratelimit.banner','Too many requests — pausing for {{n}}s',{n:remaining})
                        : t('upstream.banner','Tesla upstream unavailable — retry in {{n}}s',{n:remaining}).
  • remaining = max(0, ceil((expiresAt - now)/1000)); a 1s setInterval ticks while visible.
  • "Retry now" (t('ratelimit.retry')) — disabled while remaining>0; on click setState(null) +
    qc.invalidateQueries() (every query).
  • dismiss X (aria-label t('common.dismiss')) — setState(null).
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (the strings) + useQueryClient (the retry invalidation); the two
  events are the data mechanism. No fetch.
Shared components: web imports `Button` (→ TSButton). Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys extracted from source (verbatim): ratelimit.banner, upstream.banner, ratelimit.retry,
  common.dismiss — all reproduced one-for-one, with the i18next `{{n}}` rewritten to the native `{n}` token.
Existing native — COLLISION CHECK: the sibling surface `RateLimitStatusPanel` (feature-views 0038)
  already owns the public types RateLimitProjection / RateLimitSource / RateLimitTelemetry /
  RateLimitInput / RateLimitResolved / RateLimitSeverity / RateLimitAccessibility / RateLimitModel /
  RateLimitDuration. EVERY symbol in this surface is therefore `RateLimitBanner`-prefixed
  (RateLimitBannerKind / …Projection / …Source / …Model / …Input / …Resolved / …Countdown /
  …Accessibility / …Ticker / …QueryInvalidating, plus LiveRateLimitBannerSource etc.). Collision-checked:
  0 duplicate-symbol overlaps. (Proven below — both surfaces co-compiled in the same app-target Swift
  batch with no "ambiguous/redeclaration" error.)

=== REASONING ===
- The web banner is event-driven + self-owning; the prompt requires a production-polished native surface
  reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and i18n, with every state visible (no blank box). Chosen
  architecture mirrors the canonical P4 leaf (AiLimitBanner 0025 + AchievementUnlockListener 0112):
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): RateLimitBannerKind (kind→icon + message key/fallback),
    RateLimitBannerCountdown (initial/tick/isRetryEnabled + "{n}" interpolation = the web `remaining`
    arithmetic), RateLimitBannerCopy (the web message ternary), RateLimitBannerAccessibility (VoiceOver label).
  • Model: RateLimitBannerTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; RateLimitBannerConnection
    axis; RateLimitBannerEvent (the fired 429/503 detail); RateLimitBannerInput snapshot (event + a
    monotonic emission `sequence` + parent lifecycle); RateLimitBannerResolved + Projection
    (loading/empty/error/data, the web `if (!state) return null` → friendly empty); @Observable
    RateLimitBannerModel (drives the countdown via the ticker — reset only on a fresh emission, preserved
    on a connection-only update — one-shot stale auto-refresh, retry gated on retryEnabled →
    invalidateAll() + clear, dismiss → clear); RateLimitBannerStrings facade (table "RateLimitBanner").
  • Seams: RateLimitBannerSource protocol; LiveRateLimitBannerSource (production — observes the two
    NotificationCenter names = the native parity of `document.addEventListener`, ingests on each, the
    numeric Retry-After guard = web `typeof detail.retryAfterSec !== 'number'`); InMemoryRateLimitBannerSource
    (previews/tests); RateLimitBannerTicker (Timer 1Hz / Manual double); RateLimitBannerQueryInvalidating
    (the native parity of useQueryClient().invalidateQueries() — default posts a cross-module signal) + spy.
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests/SeamsTests.
- States rendered (no hidden surface): loading (skeleton banner row), empty (no fired event — friendly
  TSEmptyState, the native parity of the web `return null`, never blank), error (retry tile — web QueryError
  peer), data (the active warning-tinted banner: kind icon + the live countdown message + Retry-now (disabled
  while counting, web `disabled={remaining>0}`) + dismiss), and the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline
  (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- Accessibility: the banner uses accessibilityElement(children: .contain) (NOT .combine) so the message,
  the Retry-now button, and the dismiss button each stay individually focusable with their own VoiceOver
  label; Dynamic Type via tokens; reduce-motion respected via TSFadeIn; the freshness chip is a labeled button.

